# Everything here is derived from the electoral roll or produced from it. None of it goes
# into git. The repository holds the code that reads the roll; the roll itself, and every
# artefact carrying a name, a voter ID or a house number, stays on this machine.
#
# This matters more than usual for this project: the roll is a list of named voters with
# their voter IDs and their homes. It is not a test fixture.

# Extracted data and intermediate output.
# These were tracked once, in local commits that were never pushed. They are the electoral
# roll and pages rendered out of it, so they must not come back.
out/
samples/
tools/__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.csv
*.jsonl

# The app deliberately ships with no voter data in it. There is no seed to ignore because
# there is no seed: a booth is imported by the person using it, on their own phone.
android/app/src/main/assets/voters.json

# Built artefacts
dist/
android/app/build/
android/build/
android/.gradle/
android/local.properties
*.apk
*.keystore
*.jks

# Signing material, if a release key is ever added
android/keystore.properties

# Editors and OS noise
.idea/
*.iml
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Screenshots and scratch captures taken during UI work
*.png
!android/**/*.png

# Kotlin build scratch -- compiler crash logs, not source.
.kotlin/

# Tool-local dependencies. tools/ocr installs tesseract.js here rather than at the repo
# root, because the OCR harness is a standalone pipeline and pinning it separately keeps
# the Android build's Gradle tree untouched.
#
# Matched as a plain name and as the symlink itself, not only as a directory. On this machine
# tools/ocr/node_modules is a symlink to the other checkout's, and a trailing-slash rule does
# not match a symlink -- git says "beyond a symbolic link" and then helpfully lists it as an
# untracked file in every status, which is the exact moment a 200 MB dependency tree gets
# committed by accident.
node_modules/
tools/ocr/node_modules
